<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gauteng</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gauteng is the smallest but most populous province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, created in 1994 from part of the old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a> province around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/witwatersrand">Witwatersrand</a>. It contains <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannesburg">Johannesburg</a>, the country's largest city, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pretoria">Pretoria</a>, the administrative capital, and grew from the gold rush that began in 1886. Its name is a Sesotho word meaning 'place of gold'.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gauteng.jpg" alt="Gauteng" width="320" height="125" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mark Hillary · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johannesburg_skyline_2017.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
